{title: 557 - Come, Ye Thankful People}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #557 • ST. GEORGE'S WINDSOR • 7.7.8.7.7.6.7.7}
{lyricist: Henry Alford}
{composer: George J. Elvey}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 557}
{meta: tune ST. GEORGE'S WINDSOR}
{meta: meter 7.7.8.7.7.6.7.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Come, ye [C/G]thankful [Dm/A]people, [F/C]come,
[F]Raise the [C/G]song [F]of harvest [Am/E]home;
[F]All is safely [Edim]gathered [F]in,
[F]Ere the [C/G]winter storms [Gm]begin.
[C/G]God our Maker [F]doth [Gm/D]provide
[F]For our [Am]wants to [Bb]be [C7/G]supplied;
[Dm/A]Come to [Gm]God's own [C/G]temple, [F]come;
[Bb/F]Raise the [C]song [Dm/A]of [F/C]harvest [Dm/A]home!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]We ourselves [Am]are [Dm/A]God's [C]own [F/C]field,
[F]Fruit unto His praise [Gm]to [Am/E]yield;
[F]Wheat and tares [Gm]together [F]sown,
[F]Unto [C/G]joy [Dm/A]or [C/G]sorrow grown;
[C/G]First the blade and [F]then [Gm/D]the [F]ear,
[F]Then the [Am]full corn [Bb]shall [C7/G]appear;
[Dm/A]Grant, O [Gm]harvest [C/G]Lord, that [F]we
[Bb/F]Wholesome [C]grain [Dm/A]and [F/C]pure [C]may [Dm/A]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]For the [C/G]Lord [Am]our [Dm/A]God [C]shall [F/C]come,
[F]And shall [C/G]take [F]His harvest [Am/E]home;
[F]From His [Gm]field shall [Edim]purge away
[F]All that [C/G]doth [Dm/A]offend, [Gm]that [C/E]day;
[C/G]Give His angels [F]charge [Gm/D]at [F]last
[F]In the fire [Am]the tares [C7/G]to [Bb]cast;
[Dm/A]But the [Gm]fruitful [C/G]ears to [F]store
[Bb/F]In His [C]garner [F/C]evermore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Then, thou [C/G]church [Am]triumphant, [C]come,
[F]Raise the [C/G]song [F]of harvest [Am/E]home;
[F]All are safely [Edim]gathered [F]in,
[F]Free from [C/G]sorrow, free [Gm]from [C/E]sin,
[C/G]There, forever [F]purified,
[F]In God's [Am]garner [Bb]to [C7/G]abide;
[Dm/A]Come, ten [Gm]thousand [C/G]angels, [F]come,
[Bb/F]Raise the [C]glorious [F/C]harvest [Dm/A]home!
{end_of_verse}
